    {
      "id": "gqmtiwd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mitochondria generate energy in the form of ATP and are known as the 'Powerhouse of the Cell'.",
        "Lysosomes contain powerful hydrolytic enzymes and are frequently referred to as 'Suicidal Bags' of the cell.",
        "Ribosomes are non-membrane-bound organelles essential for protein synthesis in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.",
        "Rudolf Virchow added the phrase 'Omnis cellula-e cellula' meaning all cells arise from pre-existing cells."
      ],
      "id": "s0me9q8"
    },
